# The wheel over a terminal pane whose child is not tracking the mouse
# scrolls the scrollback a line per notch (Rust's `scroll_history`):
# two hundred lines from `seq`, the pane the whole screen, showing the
# tail; ten notches up bring line 200 off and the lines above in; ten
# down bring it back. (A child that tracks the mouse gets the reports
# instead — `src/app/pty_pane.zig`'s wheel test covers that.)
command view.toggle_tree
ex term seq 1 200; sleep 30
# The tab is titled by the command line, which names 200 itself.
ex rename tail
wait 1500
expect screen contains "200"
scroll 20 20 up
scroll 20 20 up
scroll 20 20 up
scroll 20 20 up
scroll 20 20 up
scroll 20 20 up
scroll 20 20 up
scroll 20 20 up
scroll 20 20 up
scroll 20 20 up
expect screen lacks "200"
expect screen contains "185"
scroll 20 20 down
scroll 20 20 down
scroll 20 20 down
scroll 20 20 down
scroll 20 20 down
scroll 20 20 down
scroll 20 20 down
scroll 20 20 down
scroll 20 20 down
scroll 20 20 down
expect screen contains "200"
